export default {"9311":"WASD drives, E enters and exits cars, space brakes, Tab shows the menu, and G resets the car. The 100 levels mix driving, stealing, parking, and elimination. Coins and speed bonuses reward chaos. The city is the playground.","trial-extreme-parkour":"Tap PLAY — it's the only control that appeared.","16987":"W A S D to move, Space to jump, C to crouch, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, R to reload, and 1-2-3 to swap weapons. P pauses. The frag-count format rewards aggression.","5311":"【电脑专属，Unity 移动端不支持，手机无法操作】WASD moves, the mouse aims and left-click shoots, the wheel swaps weapons, R reloads, space jumps, and F interacts. It is the full desktop shooter kit, immediately familiar to anyone who has played the genre. P pauses. The weapon hunt is the early game; the firefights are the late game.","save-the-girl-epic":"Tap to select one of the two offered items. Touch or mouse click — no keyboard needed.","15851":"WASD or arrow keys drive, space is the handbrake, C changes camera, F is nitro, and L toggles lights. The handbrake is the drift initiator. Drift points fund new cars, and achievements track mastery. The city is the playground.","stickman-prison-warriors":"Draw cut lines with a finger drag or a mouse click-and-drag across the hanging paper, exactly as the white tutorial hand cursor demonstrates. The scissors icon with its x3 counter tracks how many cuts the level allows, and the yellow circular arrow restarts the level when a cut goes wrong. A house icon returns to the menu, while the Pass button skips a level you cannot crack.","18674":"WASD drives on desktop, with touch controls on mobile. The trick is that slow and careful beats fast; the tracks punish speed. There is no combat and no traffic, just you against the edge. Finishing under the time limit advances you to the next level.","squid-game-hidden":"Click or tap the hidden objects listed at the side of the screen; each level has ten to find. There is no movement or aiming skill involved — this is pure observation. Misclicking costs you time, so scan before you tap, and on mobile pinch nothing — just tap precisely.","29645":"The instructions say to use the mouse or touch to control the character — tap or click to move, interact with objects, and navigate rooms. Gameplay revolves around collecting objects and keys to open doors while avoiding the Garten monsters.","24661":"Click to play: plant crops, tend them through weather changes, and harvest when ready. Selling funds upgrades that expand the operation. There is no combat and no timer; the pace is the player's. Weather is the wild card.","16477":"W A S D to move, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, wheel to change weapons, R to reload, Space to jump, P to pause. Looting is the early game — grab guns fast, fight later.","car-makeup":"Tap PLAY to start; the two panels below select the car. The shop icon top-right opens parts and styling options.","lamborghiniparking3":"Player one steers with W, A, S, D and brakes with the spacebar, per the developer. A second control scheme uses the arrow keys with keypad braking. The title screen presents a simple START entry, and the game notes phone support for touch play. Precise, small inputs matter more than speed here.","2156":"WASD moves one player, arrow keys move the other, so two players can share a keyboard. Solo players can switch between characters. The forest levels require cooperation: one character's path unlocks the other's. Puzzle logic matters more than reflexes.","run-of-life-3d-game":"On the Level 1 screen, the big orange Start button is the trigger for the run and responds to a direct tap. Two upgrade cards flank the track: GO Max Upstairs and Speed of Upstairs, each showing a gem cost of 20 and working as tappable buttons. A gem counter with a speaker icon sits at the top of the screen. The developer's official instructions list only one movement control, slide to move, which was not directly observed during testing.","red-boy-and-blue-girl-forest-adventure":"Tap PLAY on the title screen, then choose the EASY or NORMAL map. Sound and favorite toggles sit on the title.","2135":"Arrow keys or WASD drive the tractor on desktop, with on-screen buttons on mobile. Balance is the skill: too much throttle flips the tractor, too little stalls it. Obstacles and traps test the balance constantly. The tractor is slow, which makes the physics readable.","noobcraft":"The title screen keeps it simple: LETS GO starts the run, with Options and Controls menus beside it. Per the developer instructions, WASD or the left joystick moves your character, Space jumps, and the mouse or right joystick looks around. On mobile, on-screen buttons handle movement and jumping — check the Controls menu before your first attempt so you are not fumbling mid-leap.","19786":"Mouse or touch pad steers your impostor around the farm; eating food grows your family and your power. Bonuses for armor, speed, and extra impostors spawn regularly and are worth fighting over. Daily bonuses reward returning players. The last family standing wins the lobby.","candy-crush-saga-king":"Click or tap a candy, then click or tap an adjacent candy to swap them. Drag across the screen on touch devices for faster swapping. Match 4 or 5 to create special candies; combine two specials for massive clears. No keyboard needed — pure mouse or touch. Plan your moves before touching anything; the move counter is unforgiving.","garfield-rush":"Tap the restart button to start a run; the shop button (store icon) opens unlockables. Score and coin counters sit top-right.","pull-him-out-online":"Click or tap a pin to pull it out, pins slide out in the order you touch them. On desktop the mouse works, on mobile a simple tap pulls each pin. There is no undo button, so think before you pull, though restarting the level is instant. Some pins are levers that rotate sections, and those are pulled the same way with a tap.","20726":"Per the instructions: W A S D to move, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, wheel to change weapons, R to reload, Space to jump, and T for bullet time. Punches handle close range when agents get personal.","12-minibattles":"Both players share one keyboard. Player one typically uses W and S or the up and down arrows, while player two uses the remaining keys, with the exact keys shown on each mini-game's intro screen. Every mini-game uses a single button per player, so there is nothing to memorize. On touch devices, each side of the screen becomes one player's button. Matches are best of several rounds, and the intro screen always shows the controls before the countdown.","red-and-blue-stickman-huggy":"Arrow keys or WASD move the active stickman, and tapping jump twice mid-air triggers the double jump for taller ledges. On mobile, each side of the screen carries its own arrow cluster and jump button, so both brothers stay within reach. A round swap button sits dead center - one tap hands control to the other stickman instantly, no menus needed.","impostor-rescue-online":"Tap a pin with your finger to pull it and release whatever it holds back - the developer's instructions say the mouse moves the pins the same way on desktop. Tap a numbered tile on the level-select grid to open that level. The pink RESET button in the top-left corner restores the current level after a failed pull. The speaker icon in the top-right toggles sound.","5184":"Player 1 uses arrow keys with N for nitro and C for camera; Player 2 uses WASD with T for nitro and Q for camera. R restarts the level. The two maps are stunt playgrounds with ramps. Coins unlock bikes and skins.","super-mario-clicker":"You play entirely with taps, clicks, or touches, as the in-game tutorial spells out: touch the Mario to increase your money. Buy upgrades by tapping their rows in the upgrades panel, which lists each item with its star cost. Arrow buttons beside the panel scroll through more upgrades, a slider on the right adjusts the purchase multiplier, and the floppy-disk icon at the top left saves your progress.","among-space-escape":"The title screen centers on one large green play button — tap it and you are in. Per the developer, the entire game runs on two inputs: Left triggers a small jump, Right triggers a big jump. Timing which jump to use, and when, is the whole skill. There are no complex combos to memorize; two buttons carry the full game.","7290":"The instructions specify mouse control — aim and shoot with the mouse in this survivor-versus-horde setup. The pandemic-backstory framing (a lab vial, a military lockdown) sets up the standard holdout gameplay.","noob-vs-zombies-forest-biome":"【手机实测触控无反应，暂不推荐手机用户游玩】Desktop: move and jump with the keyboard; the hotbar slots are labeled 1-0 for quick item switching. Mobile: use the on-screen touch controls to move, jump, and attack.","noob-vs-pro-armageddon":"On mobile, use the on-screen arrows at the bottom left to move and the up arrow at the bottom right to jump. Tap the sword icon or the X button on the right side to attack. The TNT and SUPER TNT buttons on the right edge throw explosives. On desktop, arrow keys move and jump, Z attacks, X fires, and Space throws TNT.","14224":"Everything runs on clicks or taps: press any raised bubble and it inverts with a small pop animation. Clearing a whole toy swaps in a fresh shape, so the loop never stalls. There are no menus to learn and no settings to tweak. On desktop the mouse does it all; on touch screens a fingertip is the whole controller.","brain-test-iq-challenge":"Tap the objects on each level directly, or click and drag with a mouse on desktop — every level is touch-driven and asks you to poke at the artwork rather than press buttons. A gear icon in the top-left opens settings, a curved arrow restarts the level, and the key icon with 35 in the top-right holds the hint bank. After a solved level, the blue Next Level button moves the run forward.","parkourcraft":"LETS GO starts the run, flanked by Options and Controls menus. Per the developer instructions, WASD handles movement, Space jumps, and the mouse looks around. Mobile players get on-screen buttons instead — worth a glance at the Controls menu before the lava starts rising in your peripheral vision.","screw-nuts-snap":"Tap (or click) a screw, then tap the matching color box to place it. The booster bar offers Add Slot for extra space, Swap Box for a fresh color box, and Hammer to remove a troublesome screw.","20803":"Standard PC shooter layout per the instructions: W A S D to move, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, mouse wheel to swap weapons, R to reload, Space to jump, P to pause. Survive each round to earn new weapons from the arsenal.","dash-amp-boat":"Controls are touch-first. A big hand icon and the words 'touch to play' open Stage 1 — tap once to start the boat's run. The stage bar at the top fills as you advance toward the finish; no other buttons appeared during the playtest, so the whole loop stays one-tap simple. A settings gear sits in the corner of the start screen if you want to adjust anything first.","roshambo":"Tap one of the six hand-shaped buttons along the middle of the screen to throw. Sound and home buttons sit at the bottom, and a gamepad icon suggests controller support.","17368":"【电脑专属，需鼠标右键与滚轮，手机无法操作】Mouse controls the sniper: lock and unlock with the designated key, zoom with right-click or the wheel, and fire with left-click. Moving players are highlighted with arrows, so identification is the skill. Shooting a still player fails the mission. Patience is the weapon.","bubble-rush":"Aim with your mouse on desktop — the cannon follows your cursor — and click to fire. On mobile, drag anywhere to aim and lift your finger to shoot. Tap the cannon to swap the loaded bubble with the next one. Keyboard is optional: the left and right arrows nudge your aim, spacebar fires. Everything works with one finger on a phone.","7593":"Two-player support per the instructions: Player 1 uses W A S D, Player 2 uses the arrow keys. If the bike gets stuck anywhere, there is a respawn button to get rolling again. The goal is hitting checkpoints through rough terrain, ramps, and cliff edges.","chicken-egg-challenge":"Tap the two pink buttons — the big J button and the circle beside it — to work the chicken. The score ticks up top-right, and home/sound icons handle the rest.","15648":"WASD drives, space brakes. Drifting is the core skill: initiate slides, hold them, and chain them for points. The car roster spans premium brands, each with its own feel. Multiplayer adds human rivals to the drift battle.","super-ball-blast":"Drag your mouse or finger left and right to slide the cannon along the bottom; firing never stops and needs no trigger. Positioning is the entire game, which matters more than it sounds. Desktop has no keyboard to learn. Mobile plays identically with one-thumb dragging, even in short bursts.","18817":"The spacebar drives the action, per the instructions; swinging and mission actions flow from it. Mission selection happens up front, so you pick the challenge before swinging. There is no complex control scheme; the spacebar is the whole game. Accessibility is the point.","7112":"Player 1 uses arrow keys with N for nitro and C for camera; Player 2 uses WASD with T for nitro and Q for camera. The Free Riding map is the playground, and diamonds are the currency. Garage upgrades improve bikes. Timed races unlock new motorcycles.","roof-rails-color-stack-3d":"The runner advances on its own along the rail — no steering buttons appear on screen during the run, so lane positioning happens through touch or mouse input with the game doing the forward work. The top progress bar tracks the distance to the checkered flag. Once the finish gate is crossed, the yellow arrow button on the Level Complete screen moves the run forward.","23033":"Drive the truck with standard keys or touch, steering through checkpoints in order. Coins collected along the route unlock skins in the store. There is no combat and no timer pressure mentioned; the challenge is navigation. The truck handles like a truck, which is the point.","14517":"Arrow keys move, Z fires upward, X fires, and space triggers TNT, with a super bomb for emergencies. The labyrinths have automatic staircases, so vertical movement is built in. Combat is directional and simple. The maze is the challenge, not the controls.","16427":"Per the instructions, you can run with W A S D, the arrow keys, the mouse, or the touchscreen — whichever input you prefer. The core loop stays the same: advance during the green phase, freeze on red. The FNF characters appear as the runners you steer through the course.","15688":"W A S D to move, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, wheel to change weapons, R to reload, Space to jump, P to pause, G for grenades. The special-forces framing means a full tactical kit.","15794":"W A S D to move, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, wheel to change weapons, R to reload, Space to jump, P to pause, G for grenades. Three weapon types per the description, with exits to find on all five levels.","16426":"Click the mouse or tap the screen to work the needle, with periodic presses instead of holding, per the description. The space bar also works as an input, which is a nice desktop alternative. Shape selection happens before carving begins. The 3D camera is fixed, so there is no angle to manage.","2588":"Standard shooter layout: W A S D to move, mouse to aim and shoot, Space to jump, Shift to run, Tab for the menu. Enter opens chat for coordinating with friends in multiplayer.","kingdom-tower-defense":"Rotate to landscape — the game's own screen demands it. No other controls were visible.","ashen-watch":"Drag anywhere to move the guardian; attacks trigger automatically. Tap STORM STRIKE when it leaves cooldown, and the H/Companion button for backup. A Shop button sits top-right, with pause beside it.","1624":"On PC, drive with W (gas) and S (brake), balance your car in mid-air with A and D, trigger turbo with X, and drop bombs with Space; arrow keys cover gas, brake, and balancing as an alternative. The in-game How to Play screen lays out the same keys before the race starts. On touch screens, use the on-screen pedals and tilt controls to steer and balance.","14473":"Drag plants from the bar onto the lawn grid; sun resources fund each placement. Zombies advance in waves, and the wave tracker shows what is coming. There is no direct combat control; your strategy is the placement. The lawn is the battlefield.","grand-city-driving-2":"No controls were visible — the test stalled on the Unity loading screen.","world-conqueror":"Type a player name, then tap Adventure or World War to start. The Skins button (dice icon) opens appearance options.","17578":"WASD drives the sprint on desktop, with the mouse rotating the camera a full 360 degrees. The P key pauses. There is no combat; the verbs are run, look, and grab. Touch controls cover mobile. The timer is always visible, so route planning happens on the move.","stickman-race-3d":"The screenshots show a blue circular play button to start the race and a name entry field before each heat. On mobile, touch and drag to steer your stickman around the track. The developer notes mouse or touch as the input method, so expect click-and-drag steering on desktop as well.","18522":"Aim and shoot with the mouse or touch; the weapon-duplication happens automatically as you pass through math gates. Positioning matters less than firepower stacking. The final truck escape is the set piece to save ammo for. It is a one-thumb-friendly shooter.","motorcycle-stunts-drive":"Tap PLAY to start a run; Daily Reward claims bonus coins; SETTINGS opens options. The coin counter starts at 0.","26056":"The description frames the verbs as observe, think, guess, and infer; interaction is through clicking and typing. There is no combat and no timer mentioned; the pressure is intellectual. The room hides clues, and the word puzzle is the lock. Patience is the control scheme.","trafficcontrol-io":"Tap ENDLESS MODE to start — it's the only mode button.","25097":"WASD or the left joystick moves, the mouse or right joystick looks, and space jumps; ESC pauses. It is the standard first-person parkour kit. The maps are built for speedrunning, so momentum matters. Touch players get full joystick support.","22427":"PC shooter controls: W A S D to move, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, mouse wheel to change weapons, R to reload, Space to jump, and T for bullet time. Your mission is to protect the doll and survive until the timer runs out.","16431":"W A S D to move, Shift to walk, Space to jump, left mouse for actions, and 1-2-3 to trigger the magical auras (fiery, time, magic). Third-person perspective keeps your gargoyle visible in the magical world.","deep-space-horror-outpost":"Tap START GAME to begin; read CONTROLS first. No weapon or combat UI was visible on the menu.","temple-run-2-jungle-fall":"On desktop, press the left and right arrow keys or A and D to turn, up arrow or W to jump, and down arrow or S to slide under barriers. On touch screens, swipe left or right to turn, swipe up to jump, and swipe down to slide. Tilt controls are not used here, so every move is a deliberate swipe or keypress, which keeps the controls readable at high speed.","589":"Click or tap to shoot, with a reload mechanic between volleys. The targets are bandits and their bosses, with hostages as the no-shoot penalty. It is a pure aim game; there is no movement. Boss encounters punctuate the waves.","3d-breakfast-prapare":"Drag breakfast items into place on the 3D table — the spread is the puzzle, and placement is the only verb the screenshots show. An undo button in the top-left rolls back your last move, and a gear icon next to it opens settings. The three-star bar at the top of the screen shows your rating as you arrange. The Unity WebGL build showed a mobile-compatibility warning at launch, so desktop is the safer bet for a smooth session.","woody-block-puzzles":"Tap Play on the title screen, then pick a level node on the map. A sound toggle sits top-right; More Games links out.","29881":"Mouse click or tap to mark cards and call BINGO. The house card system means you play against the house pattern, not just random numbers. The 35-ball and 45-ball options shorten the game for quicker sessions. Pattern recognition is the skill.","holdem-royale":"The tutorial popup explains each turn: Check or Call to stay in, Raise to bet more, Fold to drop out — with 15 seconds on the clock. Six action buttons (Bet, Call, Raise, Fold, Check, All In) sit below the table, plus a −/+ stepper to size bets. The top bar carries fullscreen, trophy, help, and settings icons. Note: the game asks phones to rotate to landscape before the table appears.","knock-balls":"Tap to start each level, then aim the cannon at the stacked targets and fire. The cannon stays fixed at the bottom of the screen; every shot arcs toward the structure, and the remaining ball count sits beside the barrel.","16327":"The instructions mention keyword movement, mouse look and shooting, and C to change the character view. The headline feature is the control editor — arrange buttons and layouts to your preference before competing.","grand-city-missions":"Drive with WASD or arrow keys, press E to enter or exit vehicles, and use spacebar for the handbrake. On mobile, on-screen pedals handle acceleration and braking while you steer by dragging. The mission tracker in the corner always points to your next objective.","dogod-io":"Steer with the mouse or by dragging on mobile; your lead dog follows the pointer with a slight lag that feels charming rather than clumsy. Click, spacebar, or the on-screen button makes your pack dash, draining a little stamina. Puppies behind you mimic every move, so wide turns keep the pack together instead of stringing them out.","solitaire-8-collection":"Tap the gold PLAY button on the title screen to enter. A Golf tutorial walks you through the rules with Back and Next buttons — read it, since each variant plays differently. In Golf, tap the exposed bottom card of a column to play it onto the pile; only the last card in each column is playable. Cards are large and finger-friendly throughout.","huggy-wuggy-sewer-escape":"Tap START GAME to begin; open CONTROLS first to learn the inputs. The volume slider on the menu sets the mood.","5811":"WASD moves, mouse-1 fires, mouse-2 aims, shift sprints, ctrl crouches, space jumps, R reloads, F uses items, and G throws grenades. It is a full tactical shooter kit. The five-day structure gives the survival a campaign shape. Stealth and sprinting both matter.","35962":"Click or tap to play; the description frames it as timing-based, with the dummy running automatically and your input controlling the rhythm. There is nothing else to learn. The pace ramps with every level, so the timing window keeps shrinking. It is a one-button game in the best sense.","killmaster-secret-agent":"The trial session shows no visible touch prompts — no virtual stick, no aim reticle, no fire button appears on screen during play. What the shots do confirm is a mission flow: a big orange play button starts each level, and the results card offers home, replay, or next-mission buttons afterwards. A gear icon in the corner opens settings, and a coin counter at the top tracks gold earned. Taps and swipes are the only implied input on mobile, since nothing else is shown.","16471":"Standard shooter controls apply: mouse aims, click shoots, and movement covers the map. The description emphasizes holding the trigger and headshots, so accuracy beats spray. Level select lets you pick difficulty. Multiplayer PvP adds human unpredictability.","123-squid-game-challenge-jigsaw":"Drag jigsaw pieces across the wooden board into their slots. The back arrow returns to the level grid, and the puzzle-piece button top-right likely offers a hint or preview.","bug-crunch":"This is a tap-and-drag game: tap bugs to smack them, or keep your finger down and drag — the LOCKER screen's 'STOMP AND KEEP DRAGGING' hint and the yellow drag line under the shoe confirm continuous stomping works. The shoe follows your finger as the cursor. Between rounds, the LOCKER lets you pick footwear, and CLOSE returns you to the action.","18198":"Select your destination on the map with a mouse click or touch, then the assassination plays out. Positioning before the strike matters more than reflexes during it. Enemies alert each other, so the first target choice is strategic. Stealth positioning is the core verb.","12823":"The mouse moves your dog, and left-click boosts. Weapons evolve as you score kills and collect food, with chests dropping money for cosmetics. There is no complex aiming; positioning and timing win fights. The arena is a free-for-all, so threats come from every direction.","color-shot-throw-the-ball":"The whole game is one tap: press anywhere on the screen to throw the ball toward the ring, and the throw only lands when the colors line up. Timing is the entire skill, because a mistimed tap wastes the shot. Two large buttons anchor the bottom of the screen — a home icon to leave the session and a circular arrow to restart the run. The Unity WebGL build showed a mobile-compatibility warning during testing, so a desktop browser will give the steadier frame rate this timing game demands.","25548":"Left mouse button or touch opens the character's bar and controls the landing; the goal is to land balanced on the ground. Obstacles must be avoided mid-fall. There is no running; the skill is in the descent. Timing the landing is the core verb.","sonic-jump-fever-2":"Tap PLAY — the only button on the title screen.","home-run-master":"Our session verified only the title screen, so controls are limited to what is shown there: a speaker icon in the top-right corner toggles sound. The title art centers on a glowing target circle over the incoming ball, which suggests the swing mechanic aims through that circle — but no gameplay rendered in our test, so treat any swing instructions as unverified until you see the live game.","28965":"【电脑专属，需键盘鼠标，手机无法操作】Arrow keys or WASD move, shift runs, and the mouse looks around. It is the standard horror-exploration kit. There is no combat mentioned; the verbs are run, hide, and outsmart. The night setting means visibility is limited and sound matters.","homescapes":"Click (or tap on mobile) a gate to open it — that is the entire input the game asks for, per its own instructions. A big red Start button kicks off the level; the speaker icon in the top corner toggles sound, and the circular arrow icon restarts the level. Everything in the demo responds to simple point-and-click; no keyboard controls were observed.","moto-bike-extra":"Accelerate and brake with the up and down arrow keys, and lean the rider forward or backward with the left and right arrows - that lean is your mid-air steering and the difference between a landing and a lawn dart. On mobile, on-screen pedals handle throttle and brake while tilt-style buttons control the lean. Restarting a wrecked run is instant, which is fortunate, because the early tracks will wreck you often.","spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-swing-into-action":"The character runs automatically; tap or press Space to jump, double-tap for a double jump. The web-shooter button bottom-right fires webs. Pause top-left.","bingo-real":"Click or tap the called numbers on your card to daub them. Mouse or touch — no keyboard needed.","14544":"The mouse is the entire arsenal: click to attack with the equipped weapon and watch the ragdoll absorb it. Damage numbers tick upward, and crossing thresholds unlocks heavier hardware automatically. There is no movement to manage and no enemies fighting back. The loop is click, watch the physics flail, unlock, repeat.","22827":"【电脑专属，需键盘鼠标，手机无法操作】WASD moves, the mouse looks, space jumps, and left-click interacts, with the golden chest as the interact target at each level's end. The rules are simple: reach the chest, don't fall in lava. Ten maps means ten escalating routing puzzles. Speedrun timers reward the committed.","cannon-shooter":"Drag on the cannon to set your angle, then release to fire — the drag distance sets power, so a short pull lobs softly and a long pull launches hard. On desktop the same works with mouse press-and-drag; touch play mirrors it exactly. Two power-ups sit in the bottom corners: a bomb and a fireball, each with a visible count, and tapping one arms it for your next shot. There is no keyboard input; everything runs through aim-and-release.","princess-elsa-hidden-hearts":"No control tutorial appears in the captured session, and the input is entirely taps — touch a heart where you spot it in the illustration. The top bar shows your found count and the current level, while a timer in the corner counts down the search. A cross button exits the level and a 'more games' button sits at the bottom. Nothing else in the screenshots implies any other input.","squid-game-3d-online":"Everything runs through one large circular button: press while it glows green to run, and freeze the instant it turns red. The tested round showed no other inputs - timing that button is the entire skill. Desktop players use the same on-screen button via mouse.","23256":"Mouse or right joystick looks, WASD or left joystick moves, space jumps, and ESC pauses. The sea is the hazard, replacing lava. Ten maps escalate in difficulty. Speedrun timers reward clean runs.","15644":"The official instructions say to use the mouse: click and hold the left button to run, and steer by moving toward the direction you want. Timing is everything — you advance while the light is green and freeze the moment it turns red. Touchscreen play follows the same tap-and-hold logic.","basket-champ":"On desktop, hold the mouse button to start your shot, drag to set the arc, and release to shoot — timing and angle are everything. On mobile, swipe up from the ball to shoot, with the length and speed of your swipe controlling power. The practice court teaches the arc mechanic with zero pressure before tournaments begin.","bubble-shooter-pet-match-3":"Aim with the mouse and click to shoot bubbles, or tap and drag on mobile to aim and release. Match three or more of the same color to pop them. Swap your loaded bubble with the next one by pressing spacebar or tapping the swap button.","prison-escape-online":"Our session reached the story intro screen, which has a single NEXT button (greyed at first, then orange and tappable) to advance the comic panels. Tap or click is the input throughout — the official description frames it as a stickman escape game where you help him break out of prison. No cell or puzzle screen rendered in our test, so object-tapping mechanics are unverified.","merge-plane":"Everything is left-click or tap — no keys involved. Tap the blue buy button to purchase a plane for 50 coins once you can afford it, and use the four dark slots as your hangar grid. The Speed x2 button accelerates earnings, the SHOP button opens upgrades, and the red trash bin at the bottom clears out planes you no longer want. The Exchange panel swaps coins for propeller tokens at a posted rate of 10,000 to 1.","archer-ro":"Move with the WASD keys and click to shoot your bow. On touch screens, use the on-screen controls to move and aim. Open the build bar at the bottom to place structures, and check Upgrades to strengthen your archer.","sheep-run":"The start screen's only instruction is TAP TO START. A help (?) button sits on the left, a shop (store icon) on the right, settings below it, and a coin counter with a + button at the top.","36129":"Mouse click or tap to play; the ship fires and maneuvers under your control. Three stages with three bosses each give the game a real campaign shape. Points come from destroyed ships, and bosses are the skill checks. The top-down view keeps the action readable.","jungle-highway-escape":"Steer with the arrow keys or W, A, S, D on keyboard, per the developer's instructions. Mouse control and touch-screen steering are also supported, so mobile players can drive with their finger. The title screen shows dedicated menu buttons for sound, music, and help. Pick whichever input feels natural — the game accepts them all.","two-i-mpostor-squid-challenge":"The screenshots show no on-screen movement buttons — the round plays out on the green countdown timer at the top of the screen, with a pause button sitting in the top-right corner as the only visible control. Advance across the sandy arena while the clock runs; the timer dropping toward zero is the pressure, not a button layout.","9808":"W A S D to walk, mouse to destroy and place cubes, Tab or ESC for the menu. The description emphasizes offline play with saving, so your builds persist between sessions.","1986":"Full PC FPS controls: W A S D to move, mouse to look and fire, right mouse to aim, wheel to swap weapons, G for grenades, R to reload, F to pick up items, Shift to run, Ctrl to crouch, X to prone, V for melee. Deep keymap for a browser horror shooter.","5795":"WASD drives, space brakes, and C changes camera. The city streets are the playground, and the gopnik crowd is the flavor. Drifting is possible on the wide streets. The camera switch helps with the city layout.","formula-rush-online":"Steer with the left and right on-screen arrows (or A/D on keyboard), brake and accelerate with the pedal buttons on the right side. A live minimap in the corner traces the circuit so you can plan corners and overtakes ahead.","among-us-online-edition":"Mobile: drag the virtual joystick (bottom-left) to move your crewmate; tap the KILL, VENT, and SABOTAGE buttons (bottom-right) when playing as the impostor. Desktop: move with keyboard and interact with mouse clicks.","word-search":"On mobile a Unity notice appears first — tap OK and the game continues loading normally. From the title screen, hit the big green Play button to start a puzzle. Once the letter grid appears, drag your finger across a word in any direction to highlight it, then release to lock it in. The music-note and speaker buttons on the title toggle sound before you begin.","halloween-dentist":"The game is mouse- or tap-driven: click a tool to select it, then click the target tooth to use it. Tools unlock in order as each stage progresses, and each tool's job is labeled with a small icon. On touch screens the same tap-to-select, tap-to-apply flow applies. There is no time pressure, so exploring each tool before committing is free.","17461":"The mouse drives movement: click and hold, or tap rhythmically, to run during green light, and release the instant the light changes. There is no steering complexity; it is a straight dash. Reaction speed matters more than strategy. Touch taps work the same way.","minion-rush-2":"You play Minion Rush 2 with the mouse — or a finger tap on touch screens. Clicks drive everything the test run touched: confirming through the start screens, dismissing ads, and the revive prompt when you crash. On desktop a single mouse button does the work; on mobile the same taps carry the action. The click that matters most is the green revive button when the 'Save me' screen appears — hit it before the countdown bar runs dry.","635":"Arrow keys drive, space brakes, F is nitro, and C changes camera. ESC or Tab pauses. Stunts earn coins, and coins unlock vehicles. The handling model is realistic enough to demand mastery. Levels escalate from fun to challenging.","2575":"The instructions list full PC shooter controls: W A S D to move, mouse to aim and shoot, Space to jump, Shift to run, Tab for the menu. You pick a weapon and a map before each round. Mobile players should expect on-screen sticks and fire buttons, as is standard for this genre.","supercars-drift-racing-cars":"The developer lists WASD for driving and Space for the brake. On screen, a PLAY button starts each session. Expect W or up to accelerate, A and D to steer, S to reverse, and Space to handbrake into drifts. Touch controls likely mirror this with on-screen pedals and steering.","12635":"PC shooter setup per the instructions: WASD to move, mouse to look and shoot, right mouse to aim, wheel or 1-7 to swap weapons, R to reload, Space to jump, Shift to run. The arsenal is the point — traitors vary, so your loadout should too.","imposter-clash":"Tap or click to choose your path and deploy crewmates. Touch or mouse — no keyboard needed.","ragdoll-survivor":"A/D to move, W to jump, S to duck, F to punch, G to smash, C to block, Shift to dash, E to grab, R for super — the full key list is shown at the bottom of the screen during play.","16240":"Aim with a mouse swipe or a finger drag, then release to shoot; the description frames it as judging angle and power in one motion. Each stage moves the hole, so no two shots feel identical. There is no timer pressuring the aim. Touch players get the most intuitive version of the controls.","33893":"Per the instructions, it's mouse click or tap to play — a deliberately simple input scheme for a strategy title. Decisions are made through menus and map interactions rather than twitch inputs.","real-truck-fire-drive-sim":"In the garage menu, tap PLAY to enter the level select, where LEVEL 1 through LEVEL 4 buttons sit in a fire-station garage; BACK returns to the garage. The garage also holds STORE, DAILY REWARD, MORE GAMES and RATE US buttons. Per the official description, the keyboard scheme is WASD to drive and SPACE to brake — our session did not get past the menus into a driving scene, so treat that as the documented scheme rather than a verified one.","penguin-io":"Steer your penguin across the ice floes with touch on mobile or mouse on desktop. The bird follows your input as you move between floes and dodge rival penguins.","paper-io-2":"Steer with the mouse, WASD, or arrow keys — your block moves continuously in the direction you choose. On touch screens, drag to change direction. Your trail becomes permanent territory only when you loop back to your own land. There is no attack button; killing is done by crossing an enemy's exposed tail.","noob-vs-pro-boss-levels":"The developer's control list uses arrow keys for movement, Z to jump, X to fire, and Space for TNT, with V, B, N, and M set aside for weapon swaps — sword, AK-47, bazooka, and map. Our trial only captured the game's animated opening screen, so no touch buttons or on-screen key prompts ever appeared to confirm them. On desktop the layout reads like a classic keyboard-driven browser shooter. Check the in-game prompts once a level loads before trusting these keys.","17219":"The instructions say mouse or touchpad: aim and shoot with your pointer. Weapon upgrades come from completing math operations, a unique progression hook for the genre.","28573":"WASD or the arrow keys move, the mouse looks around, and F interacts with objects. It is the standard horror-exploration scheme. There is no combat mentioned; the verbs are explore, hide, and escape. The kindergarten setting means small spaces and bad sightlines.","2262":"Click cars to stop and start them; the mouse is the only input. Timing is everything: hold one lane too long and the queue backs up, release too early and two cars meet. The game escalates fast, so early calm is misleading. There is no pause for planning.","17799":"WASD moves, the mouse looks, and space jumps; the P key pauses. The instructions mention clicking to interact with certain elements like the airboat. It is the standard first-person parkour scheme, immediately familiar. Precision matters more than speed.","stickman-bow-clash":"Duels are turn-based: wait for the YOUR TURN banner, then drag back from your archer and release to shoot — the on-screen hint says it plainly. Longer drags mean longer shots, so judge distance before you commit. The hint also flags headshots for double damage, making aim height part of every decision. A pause button sits bottom-right if you need a breather mid-duel.","36733":"【手机实测无法游玩，WASM 加载报错，暂不推荐手机用户游玩】Mouse click or tap to steer; the snake follows your cursor. Eating food grows you, and other snakes are both prey and threat. Avoiding their attacks while cutting them off is the core skill. The arena is a free-for-all.","skyblock-3d":"On desktop, move with WASD, jump with Space, break blocks with the left mouse button and place them with the right. Number keys or the scroll wheel select hotbar slots, and E opens inventory. Touch players use a virtual joystick, tap-and-hold to mine, and tap to place. Desktop controls mirror classic sandbox games, so returning players settle in fast.","6907":"Left-click drives everything: roll the dice, buy properties, manage trades. The player-count select at the start sets the table. It is turn-based, so there is no reflex demand. The board is the interface.","kids-games-collection":"Tap one of the three game icons on the hub. A video ad plays first and becomes skippable after its countdown.","talking-tom-gold-run-online":"On the title screen: tap the big Play button to start, the speaker icon toggles sound on and off, and MORE GAMES opens the publisher's catalog. Expect the standard endless-runner tap input once the run begins — the official description has Tom running down the street collecting gold coins after a robbery. Heads-up: a full-screen video ad plays before the game loads on desktop (skippable after about 20 seconds in our session).","airport-manager-flight-attendant-simulator":"On desktop, mouse clicks do nearly everything: click passengers to check them in, drag luggage to the right belts, and tap seat rows to serve meals during the flight. Number keys 1 to 4 handle the quick radio commands for boarding calls. Touch works the same way — every station reacts to taps and short drags, so tablets feel right at home.","barbee-fashion":"Everything runs on the mouse on desktop: click wardrobe categories, click garments to try them, drag through color and pattern swatches. Hairstyles, makeup, and accessories each live in their own panels. Touch players tap the same panels, and the layout is sized for thumbs. When an outfit is ready, use the camera button to snap the photo and post it for likes.","save-the-kitten":"Tap the big yellow arrows on the left and right edges of the screen (or use the arrow keys on desktop) to walk the cat. Push movable blocks by walking into them to build a path to the kitten.","4511":"Player 1 uses arrow keys with N for nitro and B to look back; Player 2 uses WASD with T for nitro and C to look back. R restarts the level. Flying physics are the skill; the cars handle differently in the air. Nitro is for clearing gaps, not for speed.","squid-game-sniper":"Tap the play button, then choose ESCAPE PLAN or DALGONA CANDY. Sound and quality toggles sit on the menu.","17218":"WASD drives cars or the character, F enters and exits vehicles, space brakes, and Tab shows the menu. The open city means you choose the action: drive, shoot, steal, or just cruise. The tool variety is the sandbox. Freedom is the control scheme.","storm-dash":"Tap PLAY on the main menu to start an endless run, and CLAIM on the daily reward card to collect your streak coins. The menu asks players to rotate the phone sideways for the full view — in portrait, only the menus were reachable during the playtest. A gear icon opens settings, and tabs for UPGRADES, HEROES, and MISSIONS sit on the main screen between runs.","thief-puzzle-online":"The developer says to use the mouse to move the hand on PC and to touch and drag on mobile. The screenshots confirm a touch-first design with a large central play button. Drag the thief's hand along a path that avoids guards, dogs, and traps to reach the target object.","14195":"The instructions say mouse or touchpad: guide your impostor around the arena to eat food, grab bonuses like shields and speed shoes, and grow your group. Bigger groups dominate smaller ones, but a larger enemy group can eat you right back.","16053":"Mouse clicks or screen taps drive the needle; the description says you press periodically rather than holding, letting the crack meter settle between touches. Choosing the shape happens up front, and simpler outlines are the sane pick while learning. There is no movement and no camera to manage. Patience is the entire control scheme.","magic-farm-clicker":"Tap the giant jeweled seed in the middle of the field — that's the entire core loop. The bottom bar switches between SEEDS, SHOP (\"THE PIXELATED EMPORIUM\"), ACHIEVEMENTS, and STATS. A gift-box REWARD button sits top-right and a settings gear top-left.","20918":"W A S D to move, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, wheel to change weapons, R to reload, Space to jump, T for bullet time, P to pause. Loot guns early; the random map means adapting fast.","4728":"Click to open gates and choose doors; the description frames the core as door selection with trap avoidance. The mansion is the map, and each room is a puzzle. There is no combat; the challenge is choosing wisely. The butler's story gives the puzzles a warm frame.","22126":"WASD or arrow keys drive, NOS on shift for boost, R restarts position, T looks back, and C changes camera. Two-player mode splits the keyboard. Customization covers engine and visuals. The night city is the track.","17803":"Mouse clicks or touch taps drive the needle, pressed periodically to let the candy settle between touches. Shape selection comes first, with simpler forms recommended for beginners. There is no camera work. The rhythm of tapping is the skill.","plants-vs-zombies":"Everything runs on taps — the captured session never shows a keyboard or gesture hint. Tap the plant button at the bottom of the screen to buy (the tutorial highlights buying the first two Peashooters), then place them on the glowing defense tiles along the road. The bottom bar holds the economy: coin count, damage multiplier, gold multiplier, and a shop button. A hand cursor in the screenshots guides the first purchase, and the map screen lets you switch between the three area tabs at the top.","5548":"PC controls per the instructions: W A S D to move, left mouse to shoot, R to reload, F to use, Space to jump, P to pause. The loop is simple — shoot the horde, survive, unlock new weapons as you progress.","13597":"PC shooter controls per the instructions: W A S D to move, Space to jump, C to crouch, left mouse to shoot, right mouse to aim, R to reload, and 1-2-3 to swap between three weapon types. P pauses and opens the menu.","noob-vs-zombie":"The developer lists a compact keyboard setup: arrow keys to move, Z to jump, X to fire, and Space to throw TNT. Our mobile test frames showed no on-screen buttons or touch hints, so on desktop this plays as a straight arrow-key game. The jump matters most — the screenshots show grassy block platforms with ledges and drops, so learn Z's arc on flat ground before you chase anything.","among-us-crazy-gunner":"Tap the center play button to start; WEAPON and ARMOR open the loadout screens.","super-mario-bros-movie":"One input only: touch the screen or click the mouse to jump, exactly as the game's own how-to-play screen instructs. There is no left-right movement to manage — the character runs automatically, so every tap is about jump timing. No keyboard control scheme was shown in the game.","15219":"WASD drives, space brakes, and C switches the camera. The city is crowded, so the brake is as important as the accelerator. Stunts happen naturally when you push the speed. Camera changes help with tight corners."};
